 "response": {
  "text": "If you want **genuine running shoes under ₹3,000 in India**, I’d prioritize cushioning, grip, and fit over brand name. Current prices vary by size/color.\n\n### My top picks\n\n### [Decathlon Jogflow 100]()\n*₹1,599*\n\n### [Decathlon Jogflow 190.1]()\n*₹2,499*\n\n### [Adidas Throb]()\n*₹1,763*\n\n### [Campus North Plus]()\n*₹999*\n\n### [Kalenji Run One]()\n*₹999*\n\n| Shoe | Current price | Best for |\n|---|---:|---|\n| **Decathlon Jogflow 100** | ₹1,599 | ⭐ Best overall value |\n| **Decathlon Jogflow 190.1** | ₹2,499 | More cushioning / regular running |\n| **Adidas Throb** | ₹1,763 | Brand-name option |\n| **Campus North Plus** | ₹999 | Cheapest decent option |\n| **Kalenji Run One** | ₹999 | Beginner/casual running |\n\n\nThe **Jogflow 100** would be my first choice if you're running roughly **3–8 km at a time**. It has a strong combination of cushioning, grip and price, and currently has a 4.6/5 rating from over 4,000 reviews in the shopping results.\n\nIf you can spend close to the full ₹3,000, the **Jogflow 190.1 at ₹2,499** is the one I'd consider for more frequent running.\n\nThere's also evidence of **ASICS JOLT 4** dropping to around ₹2,069 in India, which is worth grabbing if your size is available; it uses an Ortholite sockliner and is a stronger choice than most ultra-budget shoes. [magicdrop.in](https://magicdrop.in/drops/best-running-shoes-under-3000?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n**One important point:** don't buy solely based on the highest rating. For running, I'd choose the shoe that fits your heel snugly, leaves about a thumb's width in front of your toes, and doesn't pinch the forefoot.\n\nIf you tell me **(1) men's or women's, (2) your usual running distance, and (3) your shoe size**, I can narrow this to the **best 2–3 pairs currently available under ₹3,000**.",
